# `wrangler types` output. Generated from each app's wrangler config by the
# `typegen` target, which declares it as an Nx output — a build artifact, not a
# committed snapshot, so there is no checked-in copy to fall behind the bindings.
#
# Being gitignored, it is invisible to Nx's file hashing, so it cannot itself be
# an input. `typegen` runs with `--env-file /dev/null` to keep its output a pure
# function of the tracked wrangler config, and both `typegen` and `typecheck`
# list that config among their inputs — that is what actually ties the check to
# the bindings. Consuming the generated `Env` (rather than a hand-written copy)
# is the other half; without it a renamed binding still compiles.
worker-configuration.d.ts
